External dependencies

Omatower Defense vendors no third-party code. Everything under game/ is original
QML written for this plugin: no sprite sheets, no fonts, no bundled libraries,
no binaries. The MIT grant above covers the whole repository.

It runs against software Omarchy already ships, and installs none of it:

  Omarchy 4+ (omarchy-shell, omarchy CLI)   MIT            Plugin host
  Quickshell                                LGPL-3.0-only  QML runtime
  Qt 6 (QtQuick)                            LGPL-3.0-only  Rendering, via Quickshell

Quickshell and Qt are used as unmodified system libraries through QML imports;
neither is redistributed here.

Runtime file access is read-only and limited to the current theme:

  ~/.local/state/omarchy/current/theme/colors.toml
  ~/.local/state/omarchy/current/theme.name

The plugin writes nothing outside its own install directory, and holds no
network, credential or user-configuration access of any kind.

Weapon names and the glyph effects they draw are modelled on Omarchy's ttfx
screensaver (MIT). Circuit layouts are stylised originals authored in
game/Balance.qml, not traced or imported data.

